From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:11:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/27] prime: make Sovereign TIDES hub-safe behind
 sovereignty-mode

S0 of SOV-P-002 (W1-W5, W11, M2, M5), from rnd/sov-004:

- sovereignty-mode = off | observe | publish, default off. Off builds
  nothing: no job or share telemetry, no sovereignty object in
  stats.json, 404 on /sovereignty*, no files, and the stats listener
  of f14bb4c. POST /sovereignty/* also needs the local token in
  data-dir/sovereignty.token.
- The detector runs in the background every sovereignty-recompute-secs
  (300) on a copy of the snapshot store. stats.json and
  /sovereignty.json serve the last pass and never hold the ledger lock
  and the engine's at once. The report publishes compute_ms.
- The score records blocks, once per job, in a ring of 2,016 persisted
  to sovereignty-blocks.jsonl. Shares only credit attested work.
- Snapshots are keyed by registered G, else by payout script, with a
  24 h idle expiry and a cap of 512 keys.
- pool_clustered zeroes a builder only when it has no canary hit.
- authored and directory appear only with the bonus on; key lookup is
  exact.

Bench at 250 gateways x 2,000 snapshots: detector pass 425 ms, and a
stats build holds the ledger lock about 1 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
