+### Sovereign TIDES (`sovereignty-mode`)
+
+`sovereignty-mode` is the master switch for the A2 code (the LZT1 attestations, the canary
+detector and the score):
+
+| Mode | What runs |
+|---|---|
+| `off` (default) | Nothing. No job or share telemetry, no `sovereignty` object in stats.json, 404 on `/sovereignty*`, no files. This is the Prime from before A2 (`f14bb4c`). |
+| `observe` | Job snapshots, attestations and blocks are recorded. The detector runs in the background every `sovereignty-recompute-secs` (default 300) on a copy of its store, never under the ledger lock; stats.json and `GET /sovereignty.json` serve the last pass (`compute_ms`, `computed_at`), with `published: false`. |
+| `publish` | As `observe`, with `published: true` for the pool site. |
+
+`POST /sovereignty/{register,attest}` need the mode on and the token from
+`data-dir/sovereignty.token` in an `X-Sovereignty-Token` header; the other POSTs (snapshot,
+canary, credit, observe, apply-bonus) also need `sovereignty-demo = true` (local rnd only).
+`sovereignty-bonus` pays nothing unless the mode is on. `authored` and `directory` (payout
+addresses) appear in the report only with the bonus on; node addresses never do.
+
+Snapshots are kept per registered `G`, else per payout script (stock `datum_gateway` makes a new
+`G` at every start), at most 2,000 per key and 512 keys, and a key unseen for 24 h is dropped.
+
+**Rollback trap (M1).** `Config` refuses unknown keys, so a Prime older than this one does not
+start with any `sovereignty-*` key in `prime.toml`. Ship the binary first with no new key (the
+mode defaults to `off`), upgrade the standby's binary before adding a key, and keep
+`prime.toml.pre-sov-<stage>` next to each change so a binary rollback can take the old toml
+with it.
+
